# Redux & Data Fetching

**ALL data fetching in Redux slices via `createApiThunk` (`client/lib/portalThunk.ts`) + the shared `api` axios instance. NEVER in components.**

```typescript
// ✅ slice
export const fetchData = createApiThunk("slice/fetchData", async () => (await api.get("/endpoint")).data);

// ✅ component
dispatch(fetchData());
const { data, loading } = useAppSelector((s) => s.mySlice);
```

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER
useEffect(() => {
  axios.get("/api/...").then((res) => setData(res.data));
}, []);
```

- Hooks: `useAppDispatch` / `useAppSelector` from `client/store/hooks.ts`
- Axios only from slices — never raw `fetch` for app APIs
- Surface errors with `formatAxiosError` from `client/lib/api.ts` in `rejectWithValue`
- Shared state belongs in the store, not component-local state
- `createApiThunk` turns API errors into `rejectWithValue(i18nKey)` and dispatches `sessionExpired()` on 401
- One-off results used by a single screen may use `dispatch(thunk(arg)).unwrap()` + local state — the request still goes through a slice thunk
- Grids: add one line to `client/store/slices/grids.ts` (`createGridSlice`) and render `<ServerGrid grid="…">`
- `X-Tenant-Id` is set automatically by `client/lib/api.ts` from the active workspace for `/app/*` calls
